---
import ReynoldsLayout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';

const lastUpdated = '10 August 2026';
---

<ReynoldsLayout
  title="Terms & Conditions | Reynolds Dryline Website Rules"
  description="Read Reynolds Dryline website terms covering acceptable use, intellectual property and liability for visitors to www.reynoldsdryline.co.uk today."
  canonical="https://www.reynoldsdryline.co.uk/terms"
>
  <PageHero
    title="Terms & Conditions"
    subtitle="Terms of use for the Reynolds Dryline website."
    breadcrumb="Legal"
  />

  <section class="rd-section rd-section--surface px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto prose prose-gray">
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 !mb-8">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <h2>1. About these terms</h2>
      <p>
        These terms apply to your use of <strong>www.reynoldsdryline.co.uk</strong> (the “Site”), operated by
        <strong>L. Reynolds (Building Systems) Limited</strong>, trading as <strong>Reynolds Dryline</strong>
        (“we”, “us”, “our”).
      </p>
      <p>
        By using the Site you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please stop using the Site.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Using the Site</h2>
      <p>You agree to use the Site only for lawful purposes. You must not:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Attempt to gain unauthorised access to the Site, server or related systems</li>
        <li>Misuse forms (including submitting spam or malicious content)</li>
        <li>Copy, scrape or reuse Site content at scale without our permission</li>
        <li>Interfere with the Site’s security or availability</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Website information</h2>
      <p>
        Content on the Site is provided for general information about our services and projects.
        Project values, descriptions, images and status information may change and should not be relied
        on as a formal offer or specification.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing on the Site creates a contract for works unless agreed separately in writing.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Enquiries and applications</h2>
      <p>
        Contact and careers forms are provided so you can get in touch or apply for roles. Submitting a
        form does not guarantee a response within a set time, or that an application will progress.
      </p>
      <p>
        How we handle personal information is explained in our
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        Text, images, logos, branding, layout and other content on the Site belong to Reynolds Dryline
        or our licensors. You may view and print pages for personal or internal business reference, but
        you may not copy, modify, distribute or commercially exploit Site content without our prior written
        consent.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Third-party links and maps</h2>
      <p>
        The Site may link to third-party websites (for example LinkedIn or Instagram) and may load map
        tiles or fonts from third-party services. We are not responsible for the content, availability or
        privacy practices of those third parties.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, we exclude liability for any loss or damage arising from
        your use of, or inability to use, the Site, or from reliance on content published on the Site.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing in these terms excludes or limits liability for death or personal injury caused by
        negligence, fraud, or any other liability that cannot be excluded under English law.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Privacy and cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Please also read our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> and
        <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>, which explain how we use personal data and cookies.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms from time to time. The “Last updated” date shows when they were last
        revised. Continued use of the Site after changes means you accept the updated terms.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of England and Wales. The courts of England and Wales have
        exclusive jurisdiction, except where mandatory consumer protections in your country of residence
        say otherwise.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms:<br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:info@reynoldsltd.co.uk">info@reynoldsltd.co.uk</a><br />
        Telephone: <a href="tel:01509816600">01509 816 600</a><br />
        Or use our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</ReynoldsLayout>
